# broiler-shared-package pin 1
#
# One package of the committed, hash-pinned feed (decision SJL-D-4 (c); milestone SJL-2.7): a shared
# library package whose home is the Broiler.Unicode repository, retained here byte for byte so that a
# restore needs no other repository's folder and no network for it. NuGet.config's package source
# mapping sends the Broiler.Unicode prefix to this directory and to nuget.org; the lock file of a project
# that references it records `content-hash`, and rule I1 holds that hash to this pin and to the
# allow-list.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. The package exactly as Broiler.Unicode's Publish workflow pushed it to nuget.org on
# 2026-10-16 (run 38952273946, its artifact nuget-packages, whose digest GitHub records and the zip as
# downloaded has), packed from `upstream-commit`; the nuspec's repository element records the same commit,
# which rule I7 reads. nuget.org serves the same package with its repository signature (.signature.p7s)
# added, and NuGet's content hash of a signed package leaves the signature out, so a restore from either
# source records `content-hash`, the base64 SHA-512 of this file's bytes. `sha256` is over the same bytes.
# (Revised 2026-10-16, when the package was published. Until then this feed held a copy packed locally
# from the same commit; the library code is the same, and the package differs in its build (the
# workflow's, on its Windows leg) and in carrying the package's README, icon and notices. The paragraph
# read: "Packed on 2026-10-16 in the Broiler.Unicode repository, from `upstream-commit`, in a clean
# worktree of it, with `dotnet pack src/Unicode.Segmentation/Unicode.Segmentation.csproj -c Release
# -p:Version=0.1.0-preview.4 -p:PackageVersion=0.1.0-preview.4 -p:ContinuousIntegrationBuild=true`. The
# nuspec's repository element records the same commit, which rule I7 reads. `content-hash` is NuGet's: the
# base64 SHA-512 of the .nupkg's bytes, which is what a lock file records. `sha256` is over the same
# bytes. It is not on nuget.org: a Broiler.VM package release that depends on it waits for its publication
# (eng/verify-feed.ps1), and the pin is then taken again from the published package, as
# Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms' pins were." The identity lines read: content-hash
# isy48tsvEepWMNioqobvVQfIHlRmFUkskubW5TUfULWSBOlAuy5tPbrUQTL7FhTZ2O8dxahljb2hJQ/ADrik5Q==, sha256
# f9e56e606f57e108b62fd9363d5413976a3394450c044c6df147dffbec8a1d3a.)
#
# WHAT IT IS. The optional segmentation package of the Unicode area (milestone SJL-7.2; Broiler.VM's
# JSD-0074), namespace Broiler.Unicode.Segmentation: UAX #29's grapheme, word and sentence boundaries and
# the word status, over the break table the caller supplies; it carries no table (decision SJL-D-6 (c)) and
# depends on Broiler.Unicode.Algorithms 0.1.0-preview.4. Admitted for PRODUCT use by
# Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript.Intl alone at SJL-7.4, so that only a root whose closure carries the Intl
# assembly carries it (rule I3). It carries no third-party component; its THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md is the
# owner's repository's, as above.

id Broiler.Unicode.Segmentation
version 0.1.0-preview.4
file Broiler.Unicode.Segmentation.0.1.0-preview.4.nupkg
content-hash C5iyHvAUD+0xArtUHX1A9k02Q3Yv6dJm5DELYC4z7SsxNd5BGvCTbfd/dTr3aVa4xSG7ugLu40Fmxzz4f4u3HQ==
sha256 c4992554dc1a19bbec1f027e4e741a423f8151ea92b9642ee81b2827106556b6
upstream Broiler-Platform/broiler.unicode
upstream-commit 6e14f93ad753094c99f0013d22269b47550ae552
